{"candidates":[{"checker_specs":[],"claim":"Filing a sandboxed Python simulation that exactly implements the specified LCG recurrence and face-mapping, returning the six face counts and total plus a calibration trace so the recurrence can be hand-verified before any tally is trusted.","counterconditions":["If the harness rejects the simulation because a requested_observables key does not resolve in the returned mapping, the proposal yields no evidence.","If the calibration trace (first ten X_n, die_n pairs) does not byte-match a hand-computed reference from the specification, the implementation is wrong and no tally from it is admissible.","If the recurrence is not run for the full 10000 terms, the counts are incomplete and the fairness claim is untestable."],"evidence_refs":[{"block":"ff5f75b13b928302","quote":"Implement the recurrence exactly as specified, run it for the full n, and RETURN the six face counts as flat observables (`count_1` .. `count_6`) plus `total`"},{"block":"153ef84da9246f5f","quote":"return the first ten (X_n, die_n) pairs so the recurrence and the face-mapping can be checked by hand against this specification."},{"block":"c6c31b919b1cd091","quote":"the exact face-count distribution of a specific pseudorandom sequence has no closed form to evaluate by hand at n=10000 terms. The only way to learn the actual counts is to run the exact recurrence, in code, and tally the results."},{"block":"1c2d18924a3064bc","quote":"the whole source is exactly one `def simulate(inputs, rng)` and nothing else, and the mapping it RETURNS is the only output that is recorded."}],"mechanism":"The generator is X_0=42; X_(n+1)=(1103515245*X_n+12345) mod 2^31; die_n=1+(X_n mod 6). A Python function computes this iteratively for n=1..10000, tallying die_n into six counters. Because 2^31 mod 6=2, the LCG outputs do not cycle through residues mod 6 with perfect uniformity over short horizons, so the exact tallies are only knowable by running the recurrence. The function al