67| and checking whether deviation <= 2*sqrt(10000*5/36) ≈ 76.38.","The simulation is deterministic; the rng argument is accepted but not used, and identical results are expected across seeds."],"model_source":"def simulate(inputs, rng):\n    x = 42\n    counts = [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]\n    cal_x = []\n    cal_die = []\n    for n in range(1, 10001):\n        x = (1103515245 * x + 12345) % 2147483648\n        die = 1 + (x % 6)\n        counts[die - 1] += 1\n        if n <= 10:\n            cal_x.append(x)\n            cal_die.append(die)\n    result = {\n        'count_1': counts[0],\n        'count_2': counts[1],\n        'count_3': counts[2],\n        'count_4': counts[3],\n        'count_5': counts[4],\n        'count_6': counts[5],\n        'total': sum(counts),\n    }\n    for i in range(10):\n        result['cal_{}_x'.format(i + 1)] = cal_x[i]\n        result['cal_{}_die'.format(i + 1)] = cal_die[i]\n    return result","parameter_definitions":[],"request_identifier":"sim_lcg_die_fairness_seed10","requested_observables":["count_1","count_2","count_3","count_4","count_5","count_6","total","cal_1_x","cal_1_die","cal_2_x","cal_2_die","cal_3_x","cal_3_die","cal_4_x","cal_4_die","cal_5_x","cal_5_die","cal_6_x","cal_6_die","cal_7_x","cal_7_die","cal_8_x","cal_8_die","cal_9_x","cal_9_die","cal_10_x","cal_10_die"],"requested_seed_set":[1],"rival_predictions":["The counts fall within two standard deviations of 1666.67, so the generator is fair by the stated criterion.","One or more counts fall outside two standard deviations of 1666.67, so the generator is unfair by the stated criterion.","The calibration trace matches hand-computed values, validating the implementation."],"simulation_mode":"sandboxed_python_v1"}]}